--TEST--
`Core\Task::map` and `Core\Task::all` are two jobs, not two spellings of one: a shape literal is not an `array` and an array literal is not a written-out shape — ADR 0072 §§ 1, 2
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 2: "a shape literal cannot express *one per element of a runtime array*
// and an array cannot carry a per-element type". That is the argument for two
// members rather than one, and this case is the argument stated as a pair of
// refusals — each member handed the other's subject.
//
// The two diagnostics differ, and that is the point rather than an accident.
// `map`'s subject is an ordinary parameter, so a shape reaching it is an
// ordinary assignability failure. `all`'s subject is read field by field
// before it has a type at all, so an array reaching it loses every field at
// once and is refused as a whole — which is the E0773 that
// `CoreTy::CallableShapeTo` exists to report.
class Probe {
    public static function subjects(): void {
        var $a = Core\Task::map({rows: fn(): int => 1}, fn(int $n): int => $n);
        var $b = Core\Task::all([fn(): int => 1]);
        echo 1;
    }
}

Probe::subjects();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `array<mixed>`, found `{rows: callable}`
   --> case.nvs:15:33
%A
error[E0773]: this argument must be written out as `{...}` at the call site
   --> case.nvs:16:33
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
